{"operations":[{"content":"def median(data):\n    \"\"\"Return the median of the data.\n\n    For an even number of values, the median is the arithmetic mean of the two middle values (as a float).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        raise ValueError(\"median() arg is an empty sequence\")\n    sorted_data = sorted(data)\n    n = len(sorted_data)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted_data[mid]\n    else:\n        return (sorted_data[mid - 1] + sorted_data[mid]) / 2.0\n\ndef mean(data):\n    \"\"\"Return the arithmetic mean of the data.\"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        raise ValueError(\"mean() arg is an empty sequence\")\n    return sum(data) / len(data)\n","expected_sha256":"f735c00283c462460c01f3608ead8758248bc7aa5ff3b13bf9dd6ec8ad352ddf","kind":"modify","path":"src/stats.py"}],"rationale":"Added the missing mean function to src/stats.py to fix ImportError in tests while keeping the median function as required."}